### gen-eq-def: the guard, and what the guard was not

The history recorded earlier in this log was wrong and is corrected here.
**`gen-eq-def` is not new in U56.** It exists at U55. One line changed:

    U55   if deriving-has (td.deriving) "Eq" | td-self-recursive td
    U56   if deriving-has (td.deriving) "Eq" | td-eq-safe        td

`td-eq-safe` is a variant body no constructor field of which names `Real`.
`Real` is out because NaN is not equal to itself. Our port already implemented
the U55 half, so this was a guard widening rather than a port.

    int-pow     all five counters EXACT, both sides 397 397 610 241
    self-host   substitutions and next-id  119599 -> 119985  = the oracle
                expr-types  UNCHANGED at 147700

**`expr-types` not moving is the proof we did it the same way** rather than
merely something similar: every span in a generated definition is synthetic and
records nothing, so a version of this that recorded spans would be a different
bug wearing the same clothes.

### It is half the feature, and the wire says so

The self-host wire did not move at all -- 2,714 of 2,869, `MISSING 1`. The
reason is exact:

    __eq_TokenKind mentions, ours      0
    __eq_TokenKind mentions, oracle   15

We generate the definition and never CALL it. Upstream rewrites an equality on
a sum into a call to the generated helper, so its copy is reachable and
survives pruning; ours is dead the moment it is made. The residual
`expr-types +216` is most likely those rewritten call sites, which carry real
spans rather than synthetic ones.

That is the next item and it is the one that touches emitted bytes.

### Three tests that were pinned to an old oracle

`cargo test` went to 3 failures, all checker mint-counts whose docstrings say
they were "read off `codexcheck` at `u56-candidate-sunday`". They were re-read
at `8570fba1` -- asked of the oracle, not updated to whatever we now produce,
which is the difference between re-pinning a test and rewriting it to match the
implementation.

In the recursive-sum test **only the two non-recursive controls moved**; every
self-recursive row is unchanged, because those already had a derived definition
at U55. That is a clean confirmation that the widening did exactly what it
claims and nothing else. 218 pass, 0 fail.
